 "details": {
  "title": "What a Difference a Day Made",
  "lead": "The tune for trumpet, set on the bars of the Fret Finder guitar arrangement’s long version, in Dick Haymes’s key, D (E for the trumpet), going up to E♭ for the last sixteen bars, concert A3 to G5. It plays in that guitar track’s time, about 76. It joins the tune with the trumpet part already on that page: its intro on the title phrase, its short answers in his rests (each picks up what he last sang), its own A section, and the last line. The tune keeps his breaths where the guitar runs, a breath at the end of each sung line, and his C♯ over E major in the bridge.",
  "facts": [
   [
    "Song",
    "María Grever (1934), English words by Stanley Adams"
   ],
   [
    "Line",
    "The tune from the lead sheet on the Fret Finder page’s chords and form, with the page’s own trumpet part in his rests"
   ],
   [
    "Key",
    "D major concert (E for the trumpet), E♭ major from bar 54 (F for the trumpet)"
   ],
   [
    "Form",
    "Intro, pickup, A, bridge, A, last part, the trumpet’s A, bridge, A and last part in E♭, the last line"
   ],
   [
    "Plays with",
    "The guitar track on the Fret Finder page (wad-long-guitar.mp3), 3:56"
   ],
   [
    "Bars",
    "The four intro bars and the pickup come first, so bar 1 of the Fret Finder page is bar 6 here"
   ]
  ]
 }
}